      "id": "fb-002",
      "question": "How are SIM bundles managed?",
      "shape": "document",
      "guard": "fix",
      "blocked_on": null,
      "asked_as": "1a1db65e-52d5-493b-a1a9-7e495005530a",
      "http_status": 200,
      "seconds": 25.56,
      "answer": "SIM bundles are managed through the SIM Cards module, which handles SIM inventory, telco relationships, APN profiles, data bundles, roaming, signal quality, and suspend/reactivate actions. It provides cost visibility and ensures communication continuity for vehicles, people, cargo, generators, and remote equipment. This module helps prevent surprise bills and silent outages by maintaining a clear mapping between SIMs, devices, assets, and countries.\n\nSource: OLIWA User Stories — this is the documented design; I can't confirm from here which parts are live.",
